  "id": "COMPOUND:15278 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Abiesadine E may interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Abiesadine E is predicted to target Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial, which in turn is a target of (2R,3S)-sulfated pterosin C and 6Beta-Hydroxyloganin, both of which are also predicted to target Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. Additionally, Abiesadine E is predicted to target Retinoic acid receptor alpha, which is a target of Rubiyunnanin C, which also targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. These findings collectively indicate that Abiesadine E may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the modulation of metabolic enzymes, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
